                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td bgcolor="slategray" valign="top" width="100" nowrap>
                <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b><span class="spnMessageText"><a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=62" title="View Raddan's Profile" onMouseOver="(window.status='View Raddan\'s Profile'); return true" onMouseOut="(window.status=''); return true">Raddan</a></span></b></font><br />
                </p>
                <p>
                <font color="000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font><br />
                <font color="000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>2 Posts</small></font></p></td>
                <td bgcolor="slategray" height="100%" width="100%" colspan="2" valign="top"><a name="55"></a>
                  <table width="100%" height="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                    <tr>
                      <td valign="top">
                      <img src="icon_posticon.gif" width="15" height="15" border="0" alt="" title="" hspace="3" /><font color="000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;12/03/2004&nbsp;:&nbsp; 14:19:39</font>
                      &nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=62"><img src="icon_profile.gif" width="15" height="15" border="0" alt="Show Profile" title="Show Profile" align="absmiddle" hspace="6" /></a>
                      &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=55&TOPIC_ID=45&FORUM_ID=7"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" width="15" height="15" border="0" alt="Reply with Quote" title="Reply with Quote" align="absmiddle" hspace="6" /></a>
                      <hr noshade size="1"></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td valign="top" height="100%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2" color="000000"><span class="spnMessageText" id="msg"> I do not have AOL IM and therefore could not PM you.  So I post here to say I hope you check Lords of Prophecy out.  We are adding good toons every day.  Exceptions are made to the minimum requirements so please do not let that deter you from applying.  We could use more of the pulling classes, although we do have a number of SK's that are amazing pet pullers.  And what guild wouldn't welcome more healing power.  Your toons would be an asset.<br /><br />While the EQ player base is in decline, LoP is growing.  It is achieving the combination family atmosphere and raiding concentration so many guilds have failed to do.  There is no "burnout" in sight in LoP.  We are flourishing in these trying times.  Why?  Because our leaders have a vision, of getting to the "end game" without sacrificing guild members along the way (most often to further their own rep in my experience).<br /><br />There is much more to be learned about LoP, including our "no drama" policy, at our website.  Check out how current and well maintained our RP system is and tell me you are not impressed!<br /><br />And for those "family" guilds out there that have seen their active numbers dwindle to can't-scrape-a-group-together levels, I urge you to speak to our officers about joining LoP en masse, so you may continue to enjoy the game with your EQ friends, while gaining the raid experience and end game zone access LoP offers.</span id="msg"></font></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td valign="bottom"><hr noshade size="1" color="slategray"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1" color="000000">Edited by - Raddan on 12/03/2004  14:22:29</font></td>
                    </tr>
